# Code-hygiene gate allowlist (consumed by cicd-suite actions/code-hygiene-check).
# Patterns are git pathspec excludes, applied to both the debt-marker scan and
# the proof-circumvention scan.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE, and that emptiness is a claim, not a stub.
#
# rsr-template-repo ships two entries here (`build/container/entrypoint.sh`,
# `tests/e2e.sh`) because it carries two scaffold files whose TODOs are
# instantiation seams rather than debt. This repository carries neither file,
# so there is nothing to exempt, and inventing an entry to match the template
# would suppress the scan for a path that has no findings yet.
#
# Adding a line here requires, per the template's own rule:
#   1. a path that actually exists in this repo;
#   2. a stated reason naming why the marker is not debt (scaffold seam,
#      generated file, or third-party code);
#   3. no widening of an existing entry to cover new ground.
# Real debt gets an issue link or is fixed. If this repo later owns genuine
# debt in a scanned path, resolve or issue-link it there — do not widen this
# list.
